<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="005" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Seed dev data plus the two negative controls</title>
    <phase>0 Foundations</phase>
    <gate>004 complete</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Data seeding; the exit condition is a gate on success criterion 2.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Follows an explicit checklist with a stated exit condition.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>medium</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>004</deps>
    <tags>dataverse,seed-data,testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Seed the data that success criterion 2 needs: the positive triple AND the two negative controls the section 8.1 checklist omits.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Seeded data proves evaluation, never reality.</role>
  <goal>A matter exists that should fire Path B, plus two matters that should NOT fire it for two different reasons.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>design.md section 8.1 lists an exit condition covering only the POSITIVE case. Success criterion 2 also requires that the rule does NOT fire when either conjunct is absent, which needs two negative controls. spec.md assumption A-3 adds them.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">Dataverse: sprk_spendsnapshot, sprk_communication, sprk_budgetrevision (spaarkedev1)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/design.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: classify the communication through the LIVE enrichment path so the classifier produces the category, not a hand-written row. This is the half most easily faked and least useful if faked, because success criterion 11 measures that same classifier.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: ISS-003 (48 sprk_event rows stranded in Draft) must be addressed before the Do lane seed is meaningful. That is task 060; do not seed the Do lane here and declare it done.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: record which rows are seeded and which are real. Seeded data proves the predicate EVALUATES; only data nobody authored to make it pass proves it FIRES on reality. Keep the two readings apart in any report.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: any test this task adds that asserts a Dataverse column list, entity name or option-set value must be paired with something touching the real schema. A consistently throwing path is a defect to diagnose, never noise to tolerate.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dev data seeding</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/schema-draft.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/security-roles.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/design.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above before touching code.</step>
    <step order="1">Create the smallest sprk_budgetrevision rows needed, per the schema: matter, prior amount, new amount, sprk_revisedon, reason, author.</step>
    <step order="2">Seed spend on a matter that already carries a budget (REAL-2026-123456.01 and .02 both do). Write sprk_spendsnapshot directly, or invoke SpendSnapshotGenerationJobHandler if it can be triggered in dev; either is acceptable now because the provenance question belongs to the connector phase, which is out of scope.</step>
    <step order="3">POSITIVE case: classify one real communication on that matter as a scope or fee change through the live enrichment path, and ensure NO sprk_budgetrevision exists inside the window.</step>
    <step order="4">NEGATIVE CONTROL 1: a matter with the classified communication present AND a sprk_budgetrevision inside the window. Path B must NOT fire.</step>
    <step order="5">NEGATIVE CONTROL 2: a matter with a budget-exceeding snapshot but NO classified communication. Path B must NOT fire.</step>
    <step order="6">Record the exit condition state in notes/: which matter satisfies the positive triple, and which two are the controls.</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="8">Record any deviation from this POML in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the live enrichment path cannot be triggered in dev, STOP and escalate rather than hand-writing the classification row. A hand-written category makes success criterion 11 unmeasurable and hides exactly the weakness design.md section 1.2 names as the conjunction weakest input.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="data">Dataverse: the positive triple plus two negative controls</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/seed-data-state.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the positive matter, when the Path B predicate is evaluated by hand, then both conjuncts hold.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given negative control 1, when evaluated, then the notExists conjunct fails because a budget revision exists in the window.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given negative control 2, when evaluated, then the exists conjunct fails because no classified communication is present.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The communication classification on the positive matter was produced by the live classifier, not authored by hand, and the record id is noted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/seed-data-state.md records which rows are seeded versus real.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>design.md section 8.1 (checklist) plus spec.md assumption A-3 (the two controls). Without the controls, success criterion 2 is only half-tested.

COMPLETED 2026-10-04. Full record: projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/seed-data-state.md. Summary:
POSITIVE = REAL-2026-123456.01 (real matter, seeded communication f00b6389-8fbf-f111-aaaf-0022482913fc classified
"Fee / rate change" via the LIVE TRIAGE-EMAIL Action through POST /api/office/save -- escalation trigger not
fired). NEGATIVE CONTROL 1 = REAL-2026-123456.02 (real matter, seeded communication 9848e2b0-8fbf-f111-aaaf-0022482913fc
classified "Scope / budget change" live, PLUS seeded sprk_budgetrevision e4e5dbe6-8fbf-f111-aaaf-0022482913fc inside
